h1 Live Exchange Rate Notifications
p This system allows clients to receive real-time notifications whenever currency exchange rates are updated.
p Notifications are emitted via Socket.IO and can be filtered by uploader, source, and currency code.

h2 Configuration
p You can enable live notifications using environment variables:

pre
    code.
        LIVE_EXCHANGE_RATE=true
        NOTIFICATION_INTERVAL=1   // Interval in minutes for checking updates

p Notes:
ul
    li `LIVE_EXCHANGE_RATE` should be set to `"true"` to enable real-time notifications.
    li `NOTIFICATION_INTERVAL` defines how often the system checks for updated rates (default is 60 minute).

h2 How It Works
p The server performs the following steps at the configured interval:
ol
    li Retrieves all unique uploaders from the currency rate database.
    li For each uploader, fetches all unique sources of rates submitted by that uploader.
    li For each source, fetches all unique currencies.
    li Retrieves the latest rate for each currency and generates a **SHA1 hash** of the data.
    li Compares the current hash with the previous hash stored in memory.
    li Emits a **Socket.IO event** only if:
        ul
            li This is the first time the event is emitted.
            li The hash of the rate data has changed (indicating an update).
    li Skips emission if the data hasn’t changed.

h2 Event Naming Convention
p Each event is named using the pattern:

pre
    code.
        uploadedBy_source_currencyCode

p Example:
pre
    code.
        admin123_Myanmar Market Price_USD
        admin123_Myanmar Market Price_USD
        admin123_Ngwe Zay_USD

h2 Client Usage Example (JavaScript)
p Connect to the server and listen for updates:

pre
    code.
        const socket = io("#{baseUrl}");

        const eventName = "admin123_Myanmar Market Price_USD";

        socket.on(eventName, (data) => {
            const currencyRate = JSON.parse(data);
            console.log("Updated currency rate:", currencyRate);
        });

h2 Notes
ul
    li The server compares hashes of the latest rate data to avoid emitting duplicate events.
    li All date fields in currency rates are handled in the **Asia/Yangon timezone**.
    li Events are emitted only if there is a **new or updated rate** for the specific uploader, source, and currency.
